From: sc7731g-frame-linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] spi: sprd-adi: power-cycle the eMMC before an SC7731G restart

A warm reset after Linux read data from the eMMC left the boot ROM unable
to read the card until a power cycle; the reset handler now cuts and
restores the card's two PMIC supplies first. See the comment.

---
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-sprd-adi.c	2026-10-27 16:46:40
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-sprd-adi.c	2026-10-27 16:46:40
@@ -482,7 +482,34 @@
 		.wdg_en = 0x800 + 0x0,		/* ANA_REG_GLB_ARM_MODULE_EN */
 		.wdg_clk = 0x800 + 0x8,		/* ANA_REG_GLB_RTC_CLK_EN */
 	};
+	struct sprd_adi *sadi = data->cb_data;
+	u32 v;
 
+	/*
+	 * Power-cycle the eMMC before the reset. A warm reset after Linux had
+	 * read data from the card left the boot ROM unable to read it ("MCI
+	 * ERF" twice on the UART, then nothing until a power cycle) -- three
+	 * times by 2026-10-27, while resets after only the partition scan came
+	 * back. The cause was never found, and pulsing the controller's eMMC
+	 * reset bit (SOFTWARE_RESET bit 3) didn't reset the card (a read right
+	 * after it still worked). What a power cycle fixes, cutting the card's
+	 * supplies fixes too: vddemmccore (VCC, LDO bit 8) and vddemmcio (VCCQ,
+	 * bit 7), the vendor DT's LDO_DCDC_PD_RTCSET 0x810 / RTCCLR 0x814 pair
+	 * (set = off, clear = on, clear wins). Off, 50 ms for the card to
+	 * drain, back on and 20 ms to settle before the watchdog fires, so the
+	 * boot ROM finds a card fresh from power-up and the LDOs on.
+	 */
+	sprd_adi_read(sadi, 0x814, &v);
+	sprd_adi_write(sadi, 0x814, v & ~0x180);
+	sprd_adi_read(sadi, 0x810, &v);
+	sprd_adi_write(sadi, 0x810, v | 0x180);
+	mdelay(50);
+	sprd_adi_read(sadi, 0x810, &v);
+	sprd_adi_write(sadi, 0x810, v & ~0x180);
+	sprd_adi_read(sadi, 0x814, &v);
+	sprd_adi_write(sadi, 0x814, v | 0x180);
+	mdelay(20);
+
 	return sprd_adi_restart(data->cb_data, data->mode, data->cmd, &wdg);
 }
 
